/-! # Every window of 1..10^9 above the first, each at the divisor count it needs

One `run_segment` a window, with the fuel set from that window's own top rather than from the top
of the range, which is what `scripts/window_plan.py` prints. Window 0 is left out because
soundness asks for `7 * B <= a` and only window 1 onwards satisfies it. Each call leaves a
kernel-checked statement that the window's survivors have no prime factor up to its own bound. -/

